    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0180" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1553: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-21T18:00:00+02:00">October 21, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 21—4:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4393. My 4339, October 16, 5 p.m.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d232-f1"/> The Foreign
                    Office this afternoon orally and it was emphasized “informally and unofficially”
                    informed the Embassy that because of the battle situation (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kampflage</hi>) in the area of operations around the
                    British Isles it was impossible to give any sort of assurance of safe-conduct
                    for an American vessel to proceed to and return from a western or southern Irish
                    port for the repatriation of American citizens from the British Isles.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
